  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe new approach is to use differential evolution (DE) for global optimization followed by local refinement with SLSQP. DE is chosen for its ability to explore large search spaces and escape local optima, while SLSQP is used for fine-tuning near promising solutions. This combination aims to surpass the current C5 value by leveraging both global exploration and local exploitation. Bottlenecks include the high dimensionality (n=120) and the non-convex nature of the problem, which DE handles better than single-phase SLSQP optimization.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nVariables: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f (h[i] \u2208 [0,1])\nConstraints: \u2211h[i] = n/2 = 60, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\nObjective: Minimize max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx over all integer shifts k\n- Objective function: \n  C5(h) = (2/n) * max\u2096 corr[k] \n  where corr = correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")\n- The smooth version: \n  smooth_C5(h,T) = [m + (1/T) * log(sum exp(T*(corr-m)] * (2/n)\n  where m = max(corr)\n- Repair function ensures \u2211h[i] = 60 and h[i] \u2208 [0,1] via:\n  project_feasible(h,n)=clip(h,0,1)+adjustment_for_sum\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nAlgorithm flow:\n- Global phase: DE with 120 variables, bounds [0,1] for all elements\n- Critical operations:\n  - Objective evaluation: corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n  - Repair: Linear adjustment/origin shift preserving length\n- Recursive repair ensures initial_guwcch\n\n4. Search choices\n- DE parameters: \n  * Population size: 20 to maintain diversity\n  * Strategy: 'best1' for balance\n  * Max iteration: 200\n  * Tolerance: 1e-6\n- Local parameters:\n  * Bounds per variable: [0,1]\n  * Constraints: \u2211h[i]=60\n  * Max iterations: 500 per candidate\n- Designed to improve by combining DE's random exploration with SLSQP's gradient-guided optimization\n\n5. Budget allocation\n- Global phase: 50% of budget (550 seconds) focusing on exploration\n- Local phase: 50% of budget (550 seconds) focusing on exploitation\n- 75% iterations are with SLSQP, ensuring convergence improvements\n\n6. Validation and checks\n- All candidates must pass:\n  1. Finite C5 value\n  2. SumConstraint: sum(h) = 60\n  3. Bounds: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n  4. Objective evaluation checks\n- Repair handles cases where these fail\n- Votes longer ops using vectorized moves\nFinalC5 computed directly ensuring validity",
